## 2. [Query Library](#2-query-library)  

- Purpose: Queries within the Query Library drive [dashboards](#10-dashboards) via [searches](#8-searches), [scheduled searches](#6-scheduled-searches) via [alert queries](#8-2-alert-queries), and [playbooks](#7-playbooks).  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/querylibrary/querylibrary.html>)  
    - Updating a query in the library updates dependent dashboards and scheduled searches automatically.  
    - Total queries: ***69***  
        - [8.1 Dashboard Searches](#8-1-dashboard-searches): ***34***  
        - [8.2 Alert Queries](#8-2-alert-queries): ***35***  

***  

## 3. [Naming Schema](#3-naming-schema)  

- Purpose: The use of a standard naming convention enables users to quickly understand the function, severity, and context of a query or component. This approach facilitates efficient identification, reuse, and troubleshooting without ambiguity.  
- *QueryType - MongoDB - Database - {Logtype} - {Logsubtype} - Name [Visualization - if any]*  
- Examples:  
    - Templates: *Template - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Investigation - Total Events [numbercard]*  
    - Searches: *Search - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Overview - Count by Tag [numbercard]*  
    - Alert Queries: *AlertQuery - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Overview - Count by Tag [numbercard]*  

***  

## 4. [Resources](#4-resources)  

- Purpose: Resources allow users to store persistent data for use in searches.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/resources/resources.html>)  
- Total: ***4***  

#### 4.1. [Lookups](#4-1-lookups)  

- Purpose: Lookup Resources are used by the *lookup* module to perform data enrichment and translation off of a static lookup table stored in a resource.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/search/lookup/lookup.html>)  
- Total: ***4***  
    - mongodb-audit-evs: MongoDB audit log field lookup.  
    - mongodb-audit-categories: MongoDB Audit tag-to-category mapping used by generated category overview templates.  
    - mongodb-audit-result-codes: MongoDB audit result code lookup.  
    - mongodb-audit-actionType: MongoDB mongo-schema audit action type catalog mapping atype/actionType values to categories, subcategories, parameter fields, result codes, and alert severity.  

***  

## 5. [Alerts](#5-alerts)  

- Purpose: Alerts notify you of potential nefarious actions that took place within and/or against your environment by tying dispatchers and consumers together.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html#alerts>)  
- Total: ***0***  

#### 5.1. [Dispatchers](#5-1-dispatchers)  

- Purpose: Dispatchers generate events. A typical dispatcher would be a scheduled search that runs on an interval; every result returned by a scheduled search is considered an event.  
    - Dispatchers = [Scheduled Searches](#6-scheduled-searches)  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html#adding-dispatchers>)  
- Total: ***35***  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - All Roles Dropped From Database [table]: Detects removal of all roles from a MongoDB database.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - All Users Dropped From Database [table]: Detects removal of all users from a MongoDB database.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Authentication Abandoned [table]: Detects incomplete or abandoned MongoDB authentication attempts.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Authentication Failure [table]: Detects failed MongoDB authentication audit events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Authentication Failure Spike By Remote IP [table]: Detects repeated failed MongoDB authentication attempts by remote IP.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Authentication Mechanism Unavailable [table]: Detects MongoDB authentication attempts using an unavailable authentication mechanism.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Cluster Parameter Changed [table]: Detects MongoDB cluster parameter changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Collection Created [table]: Detects MongoDB collection or view creation.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Collection Dropped [table]: Detects MongoDB collection or view deletion.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Collection Renamed [table]: Detects MongoDB collection rename activity.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Database - Audit - Alerts - Collection Sharded [table]: Detects MongoDB collection sharding activity.  
